    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d128">

                <pb facs="0124" n="118" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg118"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860D.00/1029: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Finland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">McClintock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Helsinki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-28T17:00:00+02:00">December 28,
                            1942—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:03 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1275. Chief of Protocol<anchor n="8" xml:id="d128-f1"/> last night informed me
                    that although annual New Year reception would not be held at President’s Palace
                    on January 1, it was expected that President’s book would be signed by
                    diplomatic representatives and that “pf”<anchor n="9" xml:id="d128-f2"/> cards
                    would be sent to Prime Minister and Foreign Minister.</p>
                <p>In view of Japanese tea party on December 8, I am not disposed to send cards to
                    Rangell or Witting unless instructed to do so by you.<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d128-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McClintock</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d128-f1" n="8" xml:id="d128-f1-content">
                <p>R. Hakkarainen.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d128-f2" n="9" xml:id="d128-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Pro forma</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d128-f3" n="10" xml:id="d128-f3-content">
                <p>No indication has been found in Department files of instructions sent in this
                    matter.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
